    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0229" n="63" xml:id="pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2611</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-13T21:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1917, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President has been prevailed upon, to sign mandate dissolving Parliament
                    which was today countersigned by newly appointed acting Premier, the General of
                    Peking Gendarmerie. Although the mandate mentions an early election of new
                    Parliament, it is probably not satisfactory to the South.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
